%U A382361 1360237114392,7629934603614,42922108890428,242099261757476,1368888000679244,7757544578196330,44054576589968260
%N A382361 Number of nonnesting permutations of the multiset {1,1,2,2,...,n,n} that avoid 123.
%C A382361 Nonnesting permutations of the multiset {1,1,2,2,...,n,n} such that if abcd is a subsequence, then a=d implies b!=c. A permutation avoids 123 if it does not contain any subsequence abc such that a<b<c. For example, 31432142 does not avoid 123 because it contains 134. 34321421 avoids 123.
%H A382361 Alois P. Heinz, <a href="/A382361/b382361.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..1290</a>
%H A382361 Eric Cowan, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.21680">Nonnesting permutations avoiding 123</a>, arXiv:2608.21680 [math.CO], 2026. See pp. 1, 2, 9.
%H A382361 Robert Dougherty-Bliss, <a href="/A382361/a382361.txt">Python program</a>, May 28 2025.
%H A382361 Sergi Elizalde and Amya Luo, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2412.00336">Pattern avoidance in nonnesting permutations</a>, arXiv:2412.00336 [math.CO], 2024.
%H A382361 Sean A. Irvine, <a href="https://github.com/archmageirvine/joeis/blob/master/src/irvine/oeis/a382/A382361.java">Java program</a> (github).
%F A382361 G.f.: 1+x*(1+U)/(2-x*(1+U)*(1+V)), where U and V are the unique formal power series satisfying U=1+3*x+x*U^2 and V=1+x*V^2. See Cowan, Theorem 1.1. - _Eric Cowan_, Oct 07 2026
